A||N||5||burdell1||Oil pan leak repair||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||03-22-2000||11:58 AM||||Is it very hard to repair an oil pan leak? How much does it cost usually to have it done  at a shop (so I know I am not getting ripped off.)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||03-22-2000||07:23 PM||||What year Fiero do you have? On my 87GT I had to bottle jack the engine so I could remove the passenger side motor mount or the oil pan won't drop out. Not a very hard job. Do a search here and don't believe the "straight forwardness" of the job in the Haynes manual if you have one. It leaves alot out!||||reg||5
Z||000002||fierospeeder||03-22-2000||10:37 PM||||I done my own 2.5l engine so it should take a mechanic less then 4 hours.<P>The alternator has to be removed, the starter, the front engine mount.  and the engine has to be up in the air.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||burdell1||03-23-2000||11:47 AM||||I have an '85 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||03-23-2000||07:33 PM||||My parts car is a 86 and I can tell by looking up at the pan I could remove that one without the hassle of the engine mount like on my 87GT. So you probably won't have the probs that I had removing it! You may have to remove the exhaust springs though if you cannot get it to drop right down. No biggy, they will go right back on again.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sluppy123||03-23-2000||08:39 PM||||Take a look at this thread   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001450.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/001450.html</A>       <P>I believe all 85-87 V-6 cradles are the same.<P>-Brian<BR>||||reg||1
